config SCHED_CASS
	tristate "Capacity Aware Superset Scheduler task placement"
	depends on m && SMP && UCLAMP_TASK_GROUP && CPU_FREQ_GOV_SCHEDUTIL && ANDROID_VENDOR_HOOKS
	help
	  Places CFS and RT tasks with the Capacity Aware Superset Scheduler
	  through the restricted scheduler vendor hooks, so the core scheduler
	  stays as it is. The foreground app (a latency sensitive group) takes
	  the faster idle CPU. Other tasks keep energy aware placement for
	  light wakeups and prefer an idle smaller CPU that fits them. The
	  busy share of the last window keeps a floor under the schedutil
	  clock for streams of short tasks.

config SCHED_SCREEN_IDLE
	tristate "Shallow CPU idle while the panel is on"
	depends on m && QCOM_PANEL_EVENT_NOTIFIER && DRM_PANEL
	help
	  Holds a CPU wakeup latency request while the primary panel is on, so
	  idle CPUs stay in their shallow state and answer a wakeup within
	  microseconds instead of leaving a power collapse. The request drops
	  when the panel blanks or enters low power, which leaves the deep
	  states to standby and always on display.
